    "start": "2026-10-01",
    "end": "2026-10-31"
  },
  "public_url": "https://github.com/dk-forge/talent-intelligence-tracker/blob/main/analysis/recall/eu/goldset-eu-2026-10.json",
  "what_this_measures": "Employers headquartered in the EU27, the United Kingdom, Switzerland or Norway that announced a funding round or a leadership change between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-31, on the announcement date, broken out by country.",
  "method": "Assembled on 2026-11-11 by one assembling agent that ran the research passes one after another, each pass enumerating its own publishers in announcement-date order inside the window and taking events in that order. No pass consulted asktherecruiter.com, this repository, the tracker database or its source registry. Discovery was public web search and the publishers' own listing pages and sitemaps, read only where the site's robots.txt allows an automated reader (sites that refuse one, including some national dailies and the main US startup wires, were not used). Every row cites the original publisher: the company's own release, an exchange or company announcement, or a named outlet's own article. Every source page was fetched and the company, date, place and amount were read on the page before the row was written, and every URL was fetched again mechanically before sealing (all answered HTTP 200). Nothing was added, edited or removed after matching began, because matching has not begun. Three country-group passes were run (the north and the British Isles, the centre and the south, central and eastern Europe and the Baltics), each for funding and for leadership, searching in the local language as well as English. No aggregator, deal database or other tracker is cited. Amounts not stated in US dollars are converted at fixed approximate rates (EUR 1.10, GBP 1.30, NOK 0.095, INR 1 crore = USD 119,000, AUD 0.66, NZD 0.58) and the detail field keeps the amount as published, so an amount check should allow for currency rounding.",
  "held_out": "Sampled independently of our own coverage: no pass saw our database, stored rows or collector list, and no row cites an aggregator, a deal database or another tracker.",
  "sampling_by_pass": {
    "europe_cee": 7,
    "europe_central_south": 24,
    "europe_north": 19
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Most countries carry only a few events, so a single country cell is an indication and not a rate.",
    "Central and eastern Europe has funding rows only: no leadership announcement from that group could be verified from an allowed publisher within the window.",
    "Exchange-listed companies' announcements were read on the press-release copy and are labelled press_release, not filing, because the copy read was the wire release.",
    "Portuguese rows come from one national business daily, which is the national_news cell almost on its own.",
    "One candidate (a Bulgarian satellite round) was left out because its only verifiable page was on a funding platform, which this family may not cite.",
    "50 of 50 items cite a publisher already in the tracker's source registry (data/feeds.csv or data/sources_catalogue.csv, checked 2026-11-11), because the publishers that allow an automated reader are largely the ones the tracker already collects from. Read the figure as recall within the publishers the tracker reads, not reach beyond them; no item comes from a publisher outside it, so this set cannot say anything about reach."
  ],
